      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><em>Waluipedia cast sheet — Kirby.</em> Built by <code>tools/build-character-sheets.py</code>, hand-authored from the article. XP ledger: level 1, power rating 16 → a level 1 Barbarian player-character sheet (a player may take this seat; the authored CR 1 stands in where the ledger is silent). Numbers are a GM-ready reading of the record, not a filed stat line; the article stays the authority. Archive date 1040 BF.</p><p><strong>The Pink Apocalypse</strong> — Dreamland (resident), Star Warriors (legacy), The Universe (maintenance)</p><p>Status: Active — goes wherever reality creaks loudest</p><p>Kirby is a pink spherical entity who lives in Dreamland and solves problems by eating them. This sounds simple until you realize the 'problems' Kirby eats include cosmic horrors, dimension-threatening nightmares, and beings that have destroyed galaxies. Kirby has saved existence multiple times while looking like a stress ball with feet. Waluigi has complicated feelings about Kirby because Waluigi respects EFFECTIVENESS, and Kirby is the most effective problem-solver Waluigi has ever encountered. Also, Kirby is TERRIFYING in ways that the cute exterior completely fails to communicate.</p><h3>Evidence</h3><ul><li><strong>Inhale</strong> — “Waluigi will list what Kirby can do, and readers should understand that this list is INCOMPLETE because nobody has found Kirby's limits: Inhale — Kirby can inhale virtually anything and either swallow it (destroying it)”</li><li><strong>Copy Ability</strong> — “Copy Abilities — When Kirby swallows something with a distinct power, Kirby gains that power.”</li><li><strong>Warp Star</strong> — “The Warp Star takes Kirby to where Kirby needs to be.”</li><li><strong>Not the Whole Story</strong> — “Waluigi will list what Kirby can do, and readers should understand that this list is INCOMPLETE because nobody has found Kirby's limits: Inhale — Kirby can inhale virtually anything and either swallow it (destroying it)”</li></ul><p>Article: <code>#/article/kirby</code> (characters). Site sheet: <code>#/sheets/kirby</code>.</p>",
        "public": ""
      }
